// spec: §3.14.2 §3.14.3
// `try!` on a value that may be none: `try` is for throwing calls; the
// help gives `??`. No mismatch follows.
// expect-error: 9:14: `try!` is for calls that throw; `xs.pop()` gives `i32 | none`, which may be none
// expect-error: help: write `xs.pop() ?? 0`, or `if let x: i32 = xs.pop() { .. }`
// forbid-error: mismatched types
// forbid-error: covers no throwing call
let xs: List<i32> = [1, 2];
let w: i32 = try! xs.pop();
